"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain reveals an intensely and homogeneously enhancing mass centered within the pineal region, measuring 1.8 x 1.5 cm. The mass compresses the tectal plate, leading to mild narrowing of the cerebral aqueduct and early dilatation of the third and lateral ventricles.\n\nImpression: Pineal region mass with secondary mass effect on the tectal plate, highly suggestive of a pineal germinoma. Recommend CSF cytology and tumor marker evaluation."
