"diagnosis": "MR evaluation of the cervical junction and brain demonstrates downward herniation of the cerebellar tonsils through the foramen magnum by approximately 8.5 mm. The cerebellar tonsils appear pointed and peg-like. There is narrowing of the CSF spaces at the level of the craniocervical junction. The ventricular system is normal in size, and sagittal sequences through the upper spinal cord show no evidence of syrinx formation.\n\nImpression: Chiari I malformation with 8.5 mm tonsillar ectopia and effacement of the CSF spaces at the foramen magnum. No associated syringomyelia or hydrocephalus is identified at this time."
