"diagnosis": "Brain MRI demonstrates a large, well-defined extra-axial fluid collection in the left middle cranial fossa, measuring 4.2 x 2.8 cm. The signal of the fluid matches cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) on all sequences, including complete suppression on FLAIR. There is mild mass effect on the left temporal lobe and mild remodeling of the overlying squamosal temporal bone, but no midline shift or ventricular compression.\n\nImpression: Large left temporal arachnoid cyst (Galassi Type II) with mild local mass effect but no herniation or obstructive hydrocephalus."
