"diagnosis": "Infant brain MRI shows severe, symmetric dilation of the lateral and third ventricles. The fourth ventricle is of normal caliber, localizing the obstruction to the cerebral aqueduct. There is significant thinning of the corpus callosum and stretching of the cerebral mantle, along with prominent transependymal CSF flow. No intracranial hemorrhage or extra-axial fluid collection is detected.\n\nImpression: Severe obstructive hydrocephalus secondary to congenital aqueductal stenosis. Immediate neurosurgical consultation is recommended."
