"diagnosis": "Brain MRI reveals multiple discrete, ovoid, hyperintense lesions on T2 and FLAIR sequences within the periventricular, juxtacortical, and infratentorial white matter. Several lesions are oriented perpendicular to the lateral ventricles, resembling Dawson's fingers. Post-contrast imaging demonstrates active enhancement of two periventricular lesions, indicating active demyelination.\n\nImpression: Findings are indicative of a demyelinating process, meeting the McDonald criteria for dissemination in space and time. Clinical correlation for pediatric-onset multiple sclerosis is advised."
