"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain demonstrates multiple, bilateral, asymmetric T2/FLAIR hyperintense lesions involving the cerebral subcortical white matter, brainstem, and deep gray matter structures. Some of these lesions demonstrate faint, patchy, non-circumscribed contrast enhancement on post-gadolinium sequences. No mass effect or midline shift is identified.\n\nImpression: Multifocal white matter and deep gray matter lesions, characteristic of acute disseminated encephalomyelitis (ADEM) given the patient's pediatric presentation and clinical course."
