"diagnosis": "Brain MRI and MR angiography demonstrate a cluster of tightly packed vascular flow voids in the left temporoparietal region, measuring 2.4 x 2.1 cm. This vascular nidus is supplied by branches of the left middle cerebral artery and drains into the superior sagittal sinus via an enlarged cortical vein. No acute hemorrhage or adjacent parenchymal edema is seen.\n\nImpression: Left temporoparietal arteriovenous malformation (AVM) without evidence of acute rupture. Recommend formal catheter angiographic correlation and neurosurgical consultation."
