"diagnosis": "Multiplanar, multisequence brain MRI reveals a well-circumscribed cyst with an enhancing mural nodule in the right cerebellar hemisphere. The cystic portion measures approximately 2.8 x 2.4 x 2.5 cm, with the solid mural nodule measuring 1.2 cm, demonstrating intense enhancement following gadolinium administration. There is moderate surrounding vasogenic edema with compression of the fourth ventricle and mild displacement of the brainstem anteriorly, although the cerebral aqueduct remains patent. No abnormal restricted diffusion or magnetic susceptibility is identified.\n\nImpression: Well-circumscribed cystic and solid enhancing lesion within the right cerebellar hemisphere, highly suggestive of a juvenile pilocytic astrocytoma. Mass effect on the fourth ventricle is present without evidence of acute obstructive hydrocephalus."
