"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain shows a large, well-circumscribed, extra-axial fluid collection in the left middle cranial fossa, measuring 4.2 x 3.0 x 2.8 cm. The fluid signal matches CSF on all sequences (T1, T2, FLAIR, DWI), showing no restricted diffusion. There is mild mass effect on the adjacent temporal lobe, but no midline shift or ventricular compression.\n\nImpression: Left middle cranial fossa arachnoid cyst (Galassi Type II) with mild mass effect on the anterior temporal lobe. No acute complications or signs of hydrocephalus."
