"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 26 weeks gestation reveals marked asymmetric dilation of the lateral ventricles. The right lateral ventricle atrial width measures 14.1 mm, indicative of moderate-to-severe ventriculomegaly, while the left atrium measures 11.2 mm. There is mild thinning of the posterior corpus callosum, although it is visible in its entirety. The sylvian fissures show appropriate opercularization for this gestational age.\n\nNo parenchymal hemorrhage, germinal matrix hemorrhage, or extra-axial fluid collections are detected. The posterior fossa structures appear normal. Impression: Significant right-sided fetal ventriculomegaly. Recommend serial follow-up ultrasounds and postnatal neurosurgical evaluation."
