"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI evaluated at 30 weeks gestation. There is a complete absence of renal tissue within both renal fossae and the fetal pelvis. No renal arteries are identified, and the fetal urinary bladder is non-visualized, consistent with anuria. Severe, near-complete oligohydramnios is present, which limits visualization of some extremities. The fetal lungs are severely small, with a calculated thoracic volume severely below the 5th percentile for 30 weeks.\n\nImpression: Bilateral renal agenesis associated with classic Potter sequence, including severe anhydramnios and pulmonary hypoplasia."
