"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 26 weeks gestation demonstrates asymmetric dilation of the cerebral ventricles. The right lateral ventricular atrium measures 13.5 mm, indicating moderate ventriculomegaly, while the left lateral ventricular atrium is within normal limits at 8.2 mm. There is no associated midline shift, subependymal heterotopia, or parenchymal destruction. The corpus callosum and cerebellar vermis appear normal for gestational age, and the sulcation pattern is appropriate.\n\nImpression: Moderate isolated right-sided fetal ventriculomegaly. Close prenatal surveillance and repeat scanning are recommended to monitor for progression."
