"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 29 weeks gestation demonstrates severe rhizomelic shortening of all long bones, consistent with a skeletal dysplasia such as thanatophoric dysplasia. The femurs are abnormally curved, resembling a \"telephone receiver\" configuration. Mild platyspondyly of the thoracic and lumbar spine is visualized. Fetal brain evaluation demonstrates a normal ventricular system (atrial width 7.2 mm) and expected sulcation patterns for 29 weeks gestation, including clear parieto-occipital sulci.\n\nImpression: Skeletal dysplasia at 29 weeks gestation, highly suspicious for thanatophoric dysplasia given severe rhizomelic limb shortening and femoral curvature."
