"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 21 weeks gestation demonstrates a dorsal neural tube defect in the lumbar spine. There is a defect in the posterior osseous elements of L4-S1 with an overlying sac containing neural tissue (myelomeningocele). Brain findings include a small posterior fossa, downward displacement of the cerebellar vermis (banana sign), and bifrontal narrowing (lemon sign), consistent with Chiari II malformation.\n\nLateral ventricles are mildly dilated at 10.5 mm. Impression: Lumbar myelomeningocele with associated Chiari II malformation."
