"diagnosis": "Multiplanar MR of the heart demonstrates patchy mid-wall to subepicardial late gadolinium enhancement (LGE) involving the lateral and inferolateral walls of the left ventricle. T2-weighted imaging and T2 mapping show increased signal intensity in these same regions, consistent with localized myocardial edema. The left ventricular end-diastolic volume is at the upper limit of normal, and the ejection fraction is mildly reduced at 51%.\n\nImpression: Dynamic MRI findings are highly characteristic of acute myocarditis. There is associated mild left ventricular systolic dysfunction without macroscopic evidence of myocardial necrosis or pericardial effusion."
