"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI demonstrates a moderate-to-large circumferential pericardial effusion, measuring up to 18 mm adjacent to the right atrium and 14 mm along the lateral wall of the left ventricle. There is associated diastolic collapse of the right atrial free wall, suggesting elevated intrapericardial pressures and impending hemodynamic compromise. The myocardium demonstrates normal signal intensity without evidence of active edema or late gadolinium enhancement. Bi-ventricular systolic function is normal, with an ejection fraction of 60%.\n\nImpression: Moderate-to-large circumferential pericardial effusion with signs of elevated intrapericardial pressure (early tamponade physiology). Close clinical monitoring and consideration of pericardiocentesis are advised."
