"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI demonstrates a moderate to large, circumferential pericardial effusion, which measures up to 18 mm in thickness adjacent to the right atrium and 15 mm adjacent to the left ventricular apex. Despite the size of the effusion, there is no evidence of diastolic collapse of the right atrium or right ventricle to suggest tamponade physiology on cine sequences. Left ventricular ejection fraction is preserved at 58%, and there is no myocardial edema or late gadolinium enhancement to suggest associated myocarditis.\n\nImpression: Moderate to large circumferential pericardial effusion without MR evidence of cardiac tamponade. The underlying myocardium is normal in size, function, and tissue characteristics."
