"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI demonstrates marked dilation and dysfunction of the right ventricle, with an end-diastolic volume index of 122 mL/m2 and an ejection fraction of 34%. Regional wall motion abnormalities are present, including dyskinesis and micro-aneurysms within the right ventricular outflow tract and inferior wall (triangle of dysplasia). Bright-blood and late gadolinium enhancement sequences reveal areas of fatty infiltration and focal fibrosis within the right ventricular free wall. The left ventricle is normal in size and function (EF 58%).\n\nImpression: Findings are highly characteristic of arrhythmogenic right ventricular cardiomyopathy (ARVC), meeting major Task Force criteria based on right ventricular volume, function, and regional wall motion abnormalities."
