"diagnosis": "Cardiac MR demonstrates mild global hypokinesia of the left ventricle with a mildly reduced ejection fraction of 48%. T2-weighted and T2-mapping sequences show patchy areas of high signal intensity in the subepicardial region of the lateral and basal free wall, indicating localized myocardial edema. Following administration of gadolinium contrast, there is pronounced, non-ischemic late gadolinium enhancement (LGE) in a mid-myocardial and subepicardial distribution within the basal-to-mid lateral wall, sparing the subendocardium.\n\nImpression: Findings are highly characteristic of acute myocarditis based on modified Lake Louise criteria, demonstrating both myocardial edema and non-ischemic late gadolinium enhancement. Mildly depressed left ventricular systolic function with trace pericardial effusion is also noted."
