"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI is performed on a 13-year-old female for evaluation of an innocent-sounding systolic heart murmur. Analysis of the biventricular chambers reveals normal volumes, wall thickness, and preserved contractility. Left ventricular ejection fraction is 62% and right ventricular ejection fraction is 59%. There are no signs of ventricular hypertrophy, regional wall motion deficits, or valvular regurgitation.\n\nNo late gadolinium enhancement or abnormal myocardial edema is visualized on specialized sequencing. Impression: Normal cardiac MRI study. No congenital, structural, or functional heart disease identified."
