"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI evaluating an 18-year-old male presenting with acute chest pain, elevated troponins, and diffuse ST-segment elevations. T2-weighted imaging and T2 mapping show focal hyperintensity in the lateral and inferolateral free walls of the left ventricle, indicating myocardial edema. Late gadolinium enhancement (LGE) imaging reveals patchy, subepicardial-to-midwall enhancement involving the same lateral and inferolateral segments, which is non-ischemic in distribution. Global left ventricular systolic function is mildly depressed with an ejection fraction of 48%.\n\nImpression: Acute myocarditis involving the lateral and inferolateral left ventricular wall based on classic Lake Louise criteria (myocardial edema and subepicardial late gadolinium enhancement). Mild left ventricular systolic dysfunction is present."
