"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI evaluates a 6-month-old infant with Tetralogy of Fallot. There is a large malalignment ventricular septal defect (VSD) measuring 9.0 mm with overriding of the ascending aorta by approximately 45%. Marked concentric hypertrophy of the right ventricle is observed. There is severe subpulmonic infundibular and valvular stenosis, with the pulmonary valve annulus measuring 5.2 mm. Main and branch pulmonary arteries are hypoplastic. Left ventricular ejection fraction is 62%.\n\nImpression: Classic anatomical findings of Tetralogy of Fallot with severe right ventricular outflow tract obstruction, hypoplastic pulmonary arteries, and marked right ventricular hypertrophy. Findings support surgical reconstruction planning."
