"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI demonstrates status post stage II single-ventricle palliation (bidirectional Glenn shunt) for hypoplastic left heart syndrome. The superior vena cava is anastomosed to the right pulmonary artery, with unobstructed, laminar forward blood flow demonstrated on velocity-encoded imaging. The single right ventricle is moderately dilated but exhibits preserved systolic function with an ejection fraction of 51%. The hypoplastic left ventricle is severely diminutive and non-functional. Mild-to-moderate neoaortic valve regurgitation is noted.\n\nImpression: Patent, unobstructed bidirectional Glenn shunt in a patient with hypoplastic left heart syndrome. Single right ventricular systolic function is adequate, with mild-to-moderate neoaortic regurgitation."
