"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI was performed on a 5-year-old male with an atypical heart murmur detected during routine screening. Multiplanar steady-state free precession (SSFP) cine sequences show normal cardiac chamber dimensions and wall thickness. There is no evidence of atrial or ventricular septal defects, abnormal valvular structure, or vascular anomalies. Global and regional biventricular systolic functions are completely normal, with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 64% and a right ventricular ejection fraction of 60%.\n\nImpression: Unremarkable pediatric cardiac MRI with no structural defects, chamber dilation, or ventricular dysfunction identified. The murmur is likely physiologic (innocent) in nature."
