"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI reveals normal pediatric cardiovascular anatomy. The ventricles demonstrate appropriate size, wall thickness, and function for a 3-year-old child. Left ventricular end-diastolic volume index is 68 mL/m\u00b2 and the right ventricular end-diastolic volume index is 71 mL/m\u00b2. Left and right ventricular ejection fractions are calculated at 63% and 60%, respectively, without focal wall motion anomalies.\n\nAll four pulmonary veins drain normally into the left atrium, and systemic venous return is unremarkable. There is no evidence of intra-atrial or intra-ventricular shunt, and late gadolinium enhancement is negative. Impression: Entirely normal pediatric cardiac MRI. No congenital structural anomalies, shunts, or functional abnormalities."
