"diagnosis": "The study was designed to evaluate an anomalous coronary artery origin in a 15-year-old female presenting with exertional syncope. MR angiography reveals that the left main coronary artery (LMCA) originates anomalously from the right coronary sinus. Importantly, the LMCA takes an interarterial course between the aorta and the main pulmonary artery, demonstrating slit-like ostial narrowing and significant acute-angled takeoff.\n\nImpression: Anomalous origin of the left main coronary artery from the right sinus of Valsalva with a high-risk interarterial course. This finding is associated with an elevated risk of myocardial ischemia and sudden cardiac death during exertion."
