"diagnosis": "Brain MRI was performed on a 29-year-old female patient, currently at 34 weeks gestation, presenting with sudden-onset seizures and severe hypertension. MR sequences demonstrate focal, patchy, and symmetric areas of T2 and FLAIR hyperintensity within the cortical and subcortical white matter of the bilateral parieto-occipital regions. There is no evidence of diffusion restriction on DWI/ADC mapping to suggest acute infarction, and no intracranial hemorrhage is identified.\n\nImpression: Imaging findings are highly characteristic of Posterior Reversible Encephalopathy Syndrome (PRES), occurring in the clinical context of preeclampsia/eclampsia. Close clinical monitoring and blood pressure management are recommended, with follow-up imaging to confirm resolution."
