"diagnosis": "Sagittal MR sequences demonstrate cerebellar tonsillar herniation extending approximately 8.5 mm below the level of the foramen magnum. The tonsils appear peg-like and pointed. There is associated effacement of the CSF spaces at the craniocervical junction. Evaluation of the cervical spine reveals a small syrinx cavity extending from C2 to C4.\n\nImpression: Chiari I malformation with cerebellar tonsillar descent of 8.5 mm and associated cervical syringomyelia. Referral to a neurosurgeon for evaluation and management is recommended."
