"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain demonstrates ventriculomegaly involving the lateral and third ventricles that is disproportionate to the degree of cerebral sulcal atrophy. There is narrowing of the sulci at the high frontoparietal convexities and enlargement of the sylvian fissures. No focal obstructive lesion of the ventricular system is identified.\n\nImpression: Ventriculomegaly disproportionate to sulcal enlargement, highly suggestive of normal pressure hydrocephalus (NPH). Clinical correlation with the triad of gait disturbance, cognitive decline, and urinary incontinence is recommended."
