"diagnosis": "Brain MRI demonstrates progressive ventriculomegaly involving the lateral, third, and fourth ventricles, which is disproportionate to the mild degree of cerebral sulcal enlargement. There is rounding of the frontal horns and a prominent flow void in the aqueduct of Sylvius on T2-weighted imaging, with narrowing of the sulci at the high convexities.\n\nImpression: Ventriculomegaly out of proportion to sulcal prominence, highly suggestive of normal pressure hydrocephalus (NPH). Clinical correlation with the triad of gait disturbance, cognitive decline, and urinary incontinence is recommended."
