"diagnosis": "Brain MRI with dedicated pituitary views reveals a well-circumscribed, solid mass expanding the sella turcica and extending suprasellarly. The lesion measures 1.8 x 1.4 x 1.5 cm and causes superior displacement and compression of the optic chiasm. There is no invasion into the cavernous sinuses, but the normal pituitary gland is compressed along the posterior sella.\n\nImpression: Pituitary macroadenoma with suprasellar extension and optic chiasm compression, clinically significant given potential visual field deficits."
