"diagnosis": "There is a large, heterogeneously enhancing, thick-walled cavitary mass in the right temporal lobe measuring 4.8 x 4.2 x 3.9 cm. The lesion is surrounded by extensive vasogenic edema, producing significant mass effect with a 7 mm leftward midline shift and partial compression of the right lateral ventricle. Areas of central necrosis and internal hemorrhage are noted.\n\nImpression: Large, aggressive, necrotic intra-axial mass in the right temporal lobe. The appearance is highly suggestive of a high-grade glioma, such as glioblastoma multiforme."
