"diagnosis": "Brain MRI demonstrates bilateral, relatively symmetric areas of high T2 and FLAIR signal intensity localized to the subcortical white matter and cortex of the parieto-occipital lobes. Minimal mass effect is associated, without restricted diffusion on DWI sequences or abnormal contrast enhancement. The findings are characteristic of vasogenic edema.\n\nImpression: Vasogenic edema in a classic parieto-occipital distribution, highly consistent with Posterior Reversible Encephalopathy Syndrome (PRES), clinically correlating with severe preeclampsia/eclampsia. Recommend clinical monitoring and blood pressure management."
