"diagnosis": "MRI and MR venography of the brain demonstrates an absence of normal flow void within the superior sagittal sinus and the dominant right transverse sinus. T1 and T2 sequences show an abnormal hyperintense clot within these venous sinuses, associated with a focal zone of venous infarction and localized edema in the right parietal cortex, containing tiny petechial hemorrhages.\n\nImpression: Superior sagittal sinus and right transverse sinus dural venous thrombosis, associated with a non-hemorrhagic right parietal venous infarction. Prompt anticoagulation is clinically suggested."
