"diagnosis": "There is marked dilation of the lateral and third ventricles, which is out of proportion to the degree of cerebral sulcal enlargement. High-convexity and midline sulci are crowded, while the sylvian fissures are disproportionately patulous. A prominent flow void is noted within the cerebral aqueduct on T2-weighted imaging, consistent with hyperdynamic cerebrospinal fluid flow.\n\nImpression: Ventriculomegaly out of proportion to cortical atrophy, presenting a pattern highly consistent with Normal Pressure Hydrocephalus (NPH). Recommend correlation with clinical triad."
