"diagnosis": "Brain MRI demonstrates a large zone of restricted diffusion involving the right insular cortex, temporal-parietal operculum, and deep gray nuclei, with corresponding ADC hypointensity. FLAIR imaging shows loss of normal cortical sulcal effacement and mild edema in the same distribution, suggesting hyperacute to acute infarction. MR angiography shows occlusion of the distal M1 segment of the right middle cerebral artery.\n\nImpression: Acute right middle cerebral artery (MCA) territory ischemic stroke with associated M1 occlusion. Immediate neurological intervention is indicated."
