"diagnosis": "MR imaging of the brain reveals a large, heterogeneous, ring-enhancing mass centered within the left temporal lobe, measuring 4.5 x 4.2 cm. The lesion exhibits central non-enhancing necrosis, thick irregular peripheral enhancement, and extensive surrounding FLAIR hyperintensity consistent with vasogenic edema. There is moderate mass effect, resulting in 8 mm of rightward midline shift and compression of the left lateral ventricle.\n\nImpression: Aggressive intra-axial left temporal lobe mass with extensive surrounding edema and mass effect, highly suspicious for high-grade glioma (such as glioblastoma). Urgent neurosurgical consult is indicated."
