"diagnosis": "Brain MRI performed 4 days postpartum demonstrates bilateral, relatively symmetric areas of high T2 and FLAIR signal intensity localized to the subcortical white matter and cortex of the occipital and parietal lobes. No restricted diffusion is seen on DWI/ADC mapping, and there is no evidence of intracranial hemorrhage or major arterial occlusion. The ventricular system and basal cisterns are within normal limits.\n\nImpression: Vasogenic edema in a distribution highly characteristic of Posterior Reversible Encephalopathy Syndrome (PRES), likely secondary to postpartum preeclampsia. Recommend clinical correlation and blood pressure monitoring."
