"diagnosis": "Dedicated MRI of the internal auditory canals shows an enhancing, ice-cream cone-shaped mass centered in the right cerebellopontine angle, measuring 2.1 x 1.6 cm. The mass extends into the internal auditory canal, causing widening of the canal. There is mild compression of the adjacent right cerebellar hemisphere and brainstem, without significant hydrocephalus.\n\nImpression: Right cerebellopontine angle dural-based enhancing mass with extension into the internal auditory canal, highly characteristic of a vestibular schwannoma (acoustic neuroma)."
