"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 27 weeks gestation demonstrates a left-sided congenital diaphragmatic hernia (CDH). Herniation of the stomach, multiple loops of small bowel, and a portion of the left hepatic lobe is visualized within the left hemithorax. This results in severe mass effect with a rightward mediastinal shift and severe compression of the left lung tissue. Calculated total fetal lung volume is reduced at 14.2 mL.\n\nIntracranial structures are normal with an atrial width of 6.2 mm and normal cerebral sulcation. Impression: Left-sided congenital diaphragmatic hernia with liver herniation ('liver-up') and associated pulmonary hypoplasia. Maternal-fetal medicine consultation is indicated."
