"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 36 weeks gestation demonstrates near-complete absence of the cerebral hemispheres. The cerebral parenchyma is replaced by a large fluid collection containing cerebrospinal fluid. Portions of the occipital lobes and lower temporal lobes are partially spared. The falx cerebri is intact. The thalami, brainstem, and cerebellum are preserved and structurally normal within the posterior fossa. The head size is normal for gestational age.\n\nThe fetal chest and abdomen are unremarkable. Impression: Hydranencephaly. This represents severe destruction of the cerebral hemispheres, likely due to a bilateral internal carotid artery occlusion or severe intrauterine insult."
