"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 30 weeks gestation demonstrates a large cystic and solid mass in the lower lobe of the left fetal lung. The mass contains multiple small cysts, the largest measuring 1.2 cm, and displays high signal intensity on T2-weighted imaging. There is associated mass effect, with mild rightward displacement of the mediastinum and heart. The remaining right lung tissue is normal in volume. No signs of fetal hydrops are present; there is no pleural effusion or ascites.\n\nFetal brain anatomy is normal, with lateral ventricular atria measuring 6.2 mm. Impression: Congenital pulmonary airway malformation (CPAM/CCAM), type II, involving the left lower lobe. Mild mediastinal shift without evidence of fetal hydrops."
