"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 21 weeks gestation demonstrates complete absence of both fetal kidneys in the renal fossae. No renal tissue is identified in the pelvis or ectopic locations. Severe oligohydramnios/anhydramnios is present, causing extreme crowding of the fetal parts. The fetal urinary bladder is not visualized, consistent with lack of urine production.\n\nThe fetal lungs are severely compressed, with calculated lung volumes far below normal limits for gestational age. Intracranial structures show compression artifacts but no overt malformations. Impression: Bilateral renal agenesis associated with anhydramnios and severe pulmonary hypoplasia (Potter sequence)."
