"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 29 weeks gestation demonstrates a large multicystic mass in the left renal fossa, consistent with a unilateral multicystic dysplastic kidney (MCDK). The left kidney is non-functional and replaced by multiple non-communicating cysts. The contralateral right kidney is normal in size, position, and parenchymal signal, showing compensatory hypertrophy. Amniotic fluid volume is completely normal.\n\nThe fetal brain demonstrates normal sulcation and gyration. The lateral ventricular atria measure 6.5 mm bilaterally. Impression: Unilateral left multicystic dysplastic kidney (MCDK) with a normal, hypertrophied right kidney and normal amniotic fluid. Fetal nephrology follow-up is recommended."
