"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 32 weeks 5 days gestation demonstrates normal third-trimester anatomical development. The cerebral hemispheres are symmetric, with advanced operculization and complex sulcation patterns, including well-defined central and precentral sulci consistent with late third-trimester transition. The lateral ventricles are slender, with the atria measuring 6.0 mm bilaterally. The corpus callosum and brainstem are morphologically normal. The cisterna magna is clear, measuring 5.9 mm, with an intact cerebellar vermis.\n\nFetal soft tissues, facial features, long bones, spine, and intra-abdominal viscera are within normal limits. Normal amniotic fluid volume and posteriorly located fundal placenta are noted. Impression: Unremarkable fetal MRI study demonstrating age-appropriate brain development and normal anatomy."
