"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 34 weeks gestation demonstrates severe shortening of all long bones of the upper and lower extremities, consistent with micromelia. The fetal thorax is extremely narrow and bell-shaped, while the abdomen is protuberant, raising high concern for pulmonary hypoplasia. The skull shows mild frontal bossing.\n\nEvaluation of the fetal brain reveals normal development for gestational age, with symmetric lateral ventricles measuring 6.1 mm and normal sulcation. Impression: Severe skeletal dysplasia with micromelia and narrow thorax, highly characteristic of a thanatophoric dysplasia or severe osteogenesis imperfecta. Genetic counseling and prenatal neonatology consultation are recommended."
