"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI evaluates a 68-year-old female with known coronary artery disease and prior stenting. There is a regional wall motion abnormality involving the mid-to-apical anterior and anteroseptal walls, characterized by akinesis. Late gadolinium enhancement (LGE) imaging reveals a subendocardial scar in the anterior and anteroseptal segments, extending to approximately 50-75% transmurality, matching a left anterior descending (LAD) coronary artery territory. The left ventricular ejection fraction is reduced at 38%.\n\nImpression: Ischemic heart disease with an established subendocardial myocardial infarction in the LAD distribution. The degree of transmural scar suggests partial viability of the affected anterior myocardium."
