"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI was performed on a 32-year-old female presenting at 4 weeks postpartum with acute onset of dyspnea and clinical signs of congestive heart failure. The left ventricle is moderately dilated, with a calculated left ventricular end-diastolic volume index (LVEDVI) of 110 mL/m2. There is global hypokinesis of the left ventricle with a severely reduced ejection fraction (LVEF) estimated at 31%. No focal myocardial edema or late gadolinium enhancement (LGE) is observed to suggest acute myocarditis or ischemic injury.\n\nImpression: Findings of ventricular dilation and severe global systolic dysfunction in the immediate postpartum period are highly consistent with peripartum cardiomyopathy. Standard guideline-directed medical therapy for heart failure is recommended with close clinical monitoring."
