"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI demonstrates a moderate circumferential pericardial effusion, which measures up to 14 mm in diastole posterior to the left ventricle. The pericardium itself is thickened and demonstrates intense late enhancement, measuring 4 mm, consistent with active inflammation. There is no evidence of diastolic collapse of the right atrium or ventricle to suggest tamponade.\n\nVentricular volumes and contractility are normal, with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 61% and no regional wall motion abnormalities. Impression: Findings are consistent with acute pericarditis and associated moderate-sized circumferential pericardial effusion. No signs of cardiac tamponade on the current study."
