"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI reveals marked thickening and redundancy of both the anterior and posterior mitral valve leaflets (Barlow's disease pathology) with prominent systolic prolapse of both leaflets into the left atrium. There is a large, eccentric regurgitant jet visible on cine sequences, consistent with severe mitral regurgitation. The left atrium is severely dilated, and the left ventricle is moderately dilated (LVEDVI 110 mL/m2) with a hyperdynamic ejection fraction of 65%.\n\nImpression: Severe mitral regurgitation secondary to bileaflet mitral valve prolapse (myxomatous mitral valve disease), with associated severe left atrial enlargement and early left ventricular dilatation."
