"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI demonstrates a discrete narrowing of the proximal descending thoracic aorta, located immediately distal to the origin of the left subclavian artery. The narrowest segment of the aortic lumen measures approximately 8 mm in diameter, compared to 19 mm at the diaphragmatic level. Velocity-encoded imaging shows a peak velocity of 3.4 m/s across the stenosis, with diastolic runoff.\n\nLeft ventricular mass index is mildly increased at 88 g/m\u00b2 indicating concentric hypertrophy, but global left ventricular ejection fraction is preserved at 62%. Large collateral vessels are visualized in the chest wall. Impression: Classic findings of coarctation of the aorta with significant hemodynamically relevant stenosis and secondary left ventricular hypertrophy."
