"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI shows marked ballooning of the left ventricular apex and mid-ventricular segments with hyperkinesis of the basal segments, manifesting a classic apical ballooning phenotype. The overall left ventricular ejection fraction is moderately depressed at 42%. There is no evidence of late gadolinium enhancement, which rules out acute myocardial infarction. Mild edema is present in the apical segments on T2-weighted sequences.\n\nImpression: Findings are typical for stress-induced (Takotsubo) cardiomyopathy, likely triggered by severe peripartum stress. There is apical and mid-ventricular ballooning and systolic dysfunction, with no evidence of coronary-related ischemic scar."
