"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI assesses myocardial viability in a 58-year-old male with a history of prior anterior myocardial infarction. The left ventricle is dilated with a thinned, akinetic anterior and apical wall. Late gadolinium enhancement (LGE) reveals transmural (>75% wall thickness) hyperenhancement of the mid-to-distal anterior wall and apex, consistent with non-viable scar tissue in the LAD distribution. The calculated LVEF is severely depressed at 38%.\n\nImpression: Severe ischemic cardiomyopathy with non-viable anterior and apical myocardial scar tissue. Depressed left ventricular systolic function with global and regional wall motion abnormalities."
