"diagnosis": "High-resolution T2 and contrast-enhanced T1 images of the internal auditory canals reveal a well-circumscribed, enhancing mass centered within the right internal auditory canal and extending into the cerebellopontine angle, measuring 1.4 x 1.1 x 1.0 cm. The mass exhibits a characteristic 'ice cream cone' appearance and causes mild displacement of the adjacent brainstem.\n\nImpression: Right vestibular schwannoma (acoustic neuroma) with intracanalicular and cisternal components. Stable to progressive findings requiring neurotology/neurosurgical follow-up."
