"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain demonstrates a crescentic, extra-axial fluid collection overlying the right cerebral hemisphere, measuring up to 1.8 cm in maximal thickness. The collection is heterogeneously hyperintense on T1 and T2 sequences, indicating a subacute to chronic subdural hematoma with areas of rebleeding. There is significant mass effect with effacement of the right hemispheric sulci, partial collapse of the right lateral ventricle, and an 8 mm leftward midline shift.\n\nImpression: Large subacute-on-chronic right subdural hematoma causing significant mass effect and an 8 mm midline shift. Urgent neurosurgical evaluation is recommended."
