"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain demonstrates a large, heterogeneously enhancing, thick-walled ring-like lesion within the right temporal lobe measuring 4.2 x 3.8 x 3.5 cm. Extensive surrounding vasogenic edema is present, manifesting as high T2/FLAIR signal extending into the adjacent white matter. There is associated mass effect, with partial compression of the right lateral ventricle and a leftward midline shift of 6 mm.\n\nImpression: Large, necrotic ring-enhancing mass in the right temporal lobe with significant mass effect. The appearance is highly suggestive of a high-grade glioma (glioblastoma) or, less likely, a solitary metastasis."
