"diagnosis": "Dedicated MRI evaluation of the sella turcica demonstrates a large, well-circumscribed, hypo-enhancing mass centered within the adenohypophysis, measuring 1.5 x 1.2 x 1.3 cm. The mass expands the sella and abuts the optic chiasm, with mild upward displacement of the chiasm structure. No cavernous sinus invasion is observed.\n\nImpression: Pituitary macroadenoma with mild mass effect and superior extension touching the optic chiasm. Visual field testing and endocrinological workup are indicated."
