"diagnosis": "MR imaging of the brain shows a large area of restricted diffusion with corresponding ADC hypointensity in the right middle cerebral artery (MCA) territory, involving the right insular cortex and frontoparietal lobes. There is associated T2/FLAIR hyperintensity in the cortical and subcortical regions, consistent with subacute ischemic infarction. Mild mass effect is noted on the right lateral ventricle, though there is no significant midline shift. Major flow voids demonstrate a lack of signal in the right M1 segment, suggestive of occlusion.\n\nImpression: Acute-to-subacute ischemic infarction in the right MCA distribution. Mild mass effect without herniation is noted, likely representing cytotoxic edema."
