"diagnosis": "There is significant dilation of the lateral and third ventricles, out of proportion to the degree of cerebral sulcal enlargement. A hyperdynamic CSF flow void is noted through the aqueduct of Sylvius. There is mild periventricular signal hyperintensity, consistent with transependymal CSF migration. The corpus callosum appears stretched and elevated.\n\nImpression: Ventriculomegaly disproportionate to sulcal thinning, indicative of normal pressure hydrocephalus (NPH) given the clinical triad. Correlate with clinical gait evaluation and high-volume lumbar puncture."
