"diagnosis": "Brain MRI demonstrates marked ventriculomegaly involving the lateral and third ventricles, which appears disproportionate to the mild degree of cortical sulcal atrophy. There is rounding of the frontal horns and bowing of the corpus callosum. Mild periventricular signal hyperintensity on FLAIR sequences is present, suggestive of transependymal flow of CSF. The fourth ventricle is only minimally dilated.\n\nImpression: Enlarged ventricular system out of proportion to cerebral atrophy, characteristic of normal pressure hydrocephalus (NPH). Clinical correlation with gait, cognitive, and urinary symptoms is suggested."
