"diagnosis": "MRI of the internal auditory canals and brain demonstrates a well-defined, enhancing mass arising from the left vestibular nerve within the internal auditory canal and extending into the cerebellopontine angle cistern. The lesion measures approximately 1.6 x 1.2 cm, producing a classic 'ice cream cone' configuration. There is mild compression of the adjacent middle cerebellar peduncle, but no significant hydrocephalus.\n\nImpression: Left-sided vestibular schwannoma (acoustic neuroma) with cerebellopontine angle extension. Otolaryngology/neurosurgical consultation is advised for management options."
