"diagnosis": "Brain MRI with susceptibility-weighted imaging (SWI) demonstrates numerous small foci of signal void (microhemorrhages) scattered throughout the cortical and subcortical regions of both cerebral hemispheres, sparing the basal ganglia and brainstem. There is also prominent periventricular leukoaraiosis and generalized cerebral atrophy, appropriate for age. No acute lobar hemorrhage or acute ischemic stroke is noted.\n\nImpression: Extensive cerebral microhemorrhages in a lobar distribution, classic for severe cerebral amyloid angiopathy (CAA). Clinical monitoring for cognitive decline and avoidance of anti-thrombotic therapy where possible is recommended."
