"diagnosis": "MR imaging of the brain reveals multiple oval, hyperintense lesions on T2 and FLAIR sequences within the periventricular and juxtacortical white matter. Several of these lesions are oriented perpendicular to the lateral ventricles, demonstrating a classic 'Dawson's fingers' configuration. On post-contrast T1-weighted sequences, two of the periventricular lesions show active ring-like enhancement, indicating active demyelination.\n\nImpression: Multiple demyelinating lesions demonstrating spatial and temporal dissemination, highly consistent with active relapsing-remitting multiple sclerosis (MS). Neurological follow-up is recommended to correlate with CSF findings and clinical criteria."
