"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain demonstrates a large, heterogeneously enhancing, infiltrative intra-axial mass in the left temporal lobe measuring approximately 4.8 x 4.2 x 4.0 cm. The mass exhibits prominent central necrotic or cystic areas with thick, irregular peripheral ring enhancement. There is extensive surrounding vasogenic edema causing significant mass effect, with subfalcine herniation to the right by 8 mm and compression of the left lateral ventricle.\n\nImpression: Infiltrative left temporal lobe mass with necrosis and significant surrounding vasogenic edema. Findings are highly suggestive of high-grade glioma, such as glioblastoma multiforme (GBM)."
