"diagnosis": "Magnetic resonance imaging of the brain shows a well-defined area of restricted diffusion in the left middle cerebral artery (MCA) territory, characterized by bright signal on diffusion-weighted imaging (DWI) and corresponding low signal on the apparent diffusion coefficient (ADC) map. This region spans the left insula, adjacent frontal operculum, and deep basal ganglia, accompanied by subtle localized gyral swelling and loss of sulcal definition on T2-FLAIR sequences. Magnetic resonance angiography (MRA) demonstrates abrupt occlusion of the M2 segment of the left MCA.\n\nImpression: Acute ischemic infarction in the left middle cerebral artery distribution. Intracranial MRA reveals occlusion of the left M2 branch, requiring immediate clinical correlation and stroke management."
