"diagnosis": "MR brain imaging reveals a well-demarcated, extra-axial mass arising from the left parietal dural convexity, measuring approximately 3.2 x 3.0 x 2.8 cm. The lesion is homogeneously hyperintense to gray matter on T2-weighted images and demonstrates intense, uniform enhancement following contrast administration, with a prominent 'dural tail' sign. There is mild localized compression of the adjacent cerebral cortex and minimal surrounding parenchymal edema.\n\nImpression: Left parietal extra-axial dural-based mass, characteristic of a benign meningioma. There is mild mass effect on the underlying brain parenchyma without significant edema or midline shift."
