"diagnosis": "MR brain imaging reveals multiple punctate foci of susceptibility blooming on SWI sequences scattered throughout the lobar cerebral cortex and subcortical white matter, particularly in the parietal and occipital lobes. There is relative sparing of the basal ganglia, thalamus, and brainstem. Moderate periventricular white matter hyperintensity of presumed microvascular ischemic origin is also present.\n\nImpression: Multiple lobar microbleeds, highly characteristic of cerebral amyloid angiopathy (CAA) in an elderly patient. Concurrent moderate chronic small vessel ischemic changes are noted."
