"diagnosis": "MR imaging of the brain reveals a wedge-shaped area of restricted diffusion with corresponding ADC hypointensity involving the cortex and subcortical white matter of the left parietal lobe, consistent with the distribution of the posterior division of the left middle cerebral artery. Faint high signal is visible on T2/FLAIR sequences within this region, representing early gyral edema. No acute intracranial hemorrhage or mass effect is identified.\n\nImpression: Acute ischemic infarction of the left parietal lobe in the left MCA territory. No associated hemorrhagic transformation is visualized."
