"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain demonstrates a crescentic, extra-axial fluid collection over the right cerebral hemisphere measuring up to 1.4 cm in maximal thickness. The collection is hyperintense on both T1 and T2-weighted sequences, indicating a subacute-to-chronic subdural hematoma containing extracellular methemoglobin. There is moderate mass effect, resulting in effacement of the adjacent right-sided sulci and a 5 mm leftward midline shift.\n\nImpression: Subacute-to-chronic right subdural hematoma with moderate mass effect and a 5 mm leftward midline shift. Urgent neurosurgical evaluation is recommended."
