"diagnosis": "MR imaging of the brain was obtained utilizing multiplanar, multisequence protocols. The cerebral hemispheres, cerebellum, and brainstem demonstrate normal morphology and signal intensity. There is no evidence of intracranial mass lesion, acute infarct, or hemorrhage. The ventricles and extra-axial fluid spaces are normal in size and configuration for the patient's age.\n\nImpression: Unremarkable MRI of the brain. No acute intracranial abnormality or structural pathology identified to explain the clinical presentation of chronic tension headaches."
