"diagnosis": "Brain MRI shows a well-circumscribed, extra-axial mass along the right parasagittal parietal convexity measuring approximately 3.2 x 2.8 x 2.5 cm. The mass is dural-based and exhibits intense, homogeneous enhancement post-contrast injection, along with a distinct 'dural tail' sign. There is mild compression of the adjacent cerebral cortex with minimal edema in the underlying brain parenchyma.\n\nImpression: Well-circumscribed, dural-based extra-axial mass along the right parasagittal parietal region, highly consistent with a benign meningioma. Mild compression of the underlying cortex is noted."
