"diagnosis": "MRI of the brain and IACs reveals a 1.8 x 1.4 cm soft tissue mass centered within the left cerebellopontine angle cistern. The lesion extends into the internal auditory canal, causing focal expansion. It demonstrates intermediate signal intensity on T1-weighted images and intense enhancement after contrast administration, with an 'ice cream cone' morphology.\n\nImpression: Intracanalicular and extracanalicular left cerebellopontine angle mass consistent with a vestibular schwannoma (acoustic neuroma). There is mild mass effect on the adjacent middle cerebellar peduncle."
