"diagnosis": "MR imaging of the brain and craniocervical junction reveals downward herniation of the cerebellar tonsils below the level of the foramen magnum by approximately 7.5 mm. The cerebellar tonsils are peg-like in configuration. There is crowding at the level of the foramen magnum, but the cervical spinal cord demonstrates normal signal with no evidence of syrinx formation.\n\nImpression: Chiari I malformation with 7.5 mm of cerebellar tonsillar ectopia and crowding at the craniocervical junction. No syrinx is noted in the visualized cervical spine."
