"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 23 weeks gestation demonstrates a lumbosacral neural tube defect with an associated myelomeningocele sac containing herniated neural elements. There is associated Chiari II malformation, characterized by a small posterior fossa, cerebellar crowding ('banana sign'), and frontal bone scalloping ('lemon sign').\n\nThe lateral ventricles are mildly dilated, with the atrium measuring 10.5 mm, reflecting mild ventriculomegaly. The cerebral sulcation pattern is normal for this early gestational age. Impression: Open lumbosacral myelomeningocele with characteristic secondary features of Chiari II malformation and mild ventriculomegaly."
