"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 32 weeks gestation reveals a large open neural tube defect in the thoracolumbar region. There is a defect in the posterior vertebral arches extending from T11 through L3, with exposure of the neural placode and an associated myelomeningocele sac. Severe Chiari II malformation is present, with downward displacement of the cerebellar vermis and medulla into the cervical canal. The lateral ventricles are severely dilated, measuring 16.5 mm on the left and 15.8 mm on the right.\n\nCortical sulcation shows mild delay, likely secondary to severe ventriculomegaly. Impression: Large thoracolumbar myelomeningocele with associated Chiari II malformation and severe bilateral ventriculomegaly."
