"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 26 weeks gestation reveals a large, multicystic dysplastic left kidney (MCDK). The left kidney is replaced by multiple non-communicating cysts of varying sizes, with no identifiable normal renal parenchyma. The right kidney is normal in size and appearance, and there is a normal volume of amniotic fluid, indicating preserved global renal function. Intracranial structures demonstrate normal sulcation for 26 weeks, and the ventricular atrium measures 6.0 mm.\n\nThe fetal chest and gastrointestinal tract are normal. Impression: Unilateral (left-sided) multicystic dysplastic kidney (MCDK) with a normal contralateral right kidney and normal amniotic fluid volume. Brain development is completely normal."
