"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 36 weeks gestation demonstrates a right-sided congenital diaphragmatic hernia (CDH). The right hemidiaphragm is deficient, with the right liver lobe and gallbladder herniating into the right chest cavity. This causes significant leftward mediastinal shift and compression of the heart and left lung. Calculated total fetal lung volume is severely reduced for gestational age.\n\nThe fetal brain shows normal cortical sulcation for 36 weeks. The lateral ventricular atria are within normal limits, measuring 6.2 mm. Impression: Right-sided congenital diaphragmatic hernia with herniation of liver and gallbladder, causing severe mediastinal shift and pulmonary hypoplasia."
