"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 25 weeks gestation. There is a large left-sided congenital diaphragmatic hernia (Bochdalek type). The stomach, small bowel loops, and a portion of the left lobe of the liver have herniated into the left hemithorax. This has resulted in a severe rightward mediastinal shift and compression of the developing lungs. The observed-to-expected total fetal lung volume is calculated at 38%, indicating severe pulmonary hypoplasia.\n\nThe fetal brain anatomy and sulcation are normal, and ventricular atrial widths measure 6.0 mm. Impression: Large left-sided congenital diaphragmatic hernia with significant mediastinal shift and severe pulmonary hypoplasia."
