"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 25 weeks gestation demonstrates posterior fossa anomalies. There is severe hypoplasia of the cerebellar vermis with rotation of the vermian remnant. The posterior fossa is enlarged, with a dilated CSF space representing a giant retrocerebellar fluid collection communicating directly with the fourth ventricle. Lateral ventricles are mildly dilated at 10.2 mm bilaterally.\n\nNo supratentorial anomalies or migration defects are detected. Impression: Findings are highly characteristic of Dandy-Walker malformation with secondary mild ventriculomegaly. Recommend prenatal pediatric neurology consultation."
