"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 25 weeks gestation reveals a significantly enlarged posterior fossa with a high-riding torcular. There is severe cerebellar vermian hypoplasia and a wide communication of the fourth ventricle with the posterior fossa fluid space. Cortical sulcation is normal for gestational age. The bilateral lateral ventricular atrial measurements are moderately dilated at 10.5 mm.\n\nImpression: Classic Dandy-Walker malformation with vermian hypoplasia, a dilated posterior fossa cyst, and associated mild bilateral ventriculomegaly."
