"diagnosis": "Fetal MRI at 22 weeks gestation reveals lobar holoprosencephaly. There is incomplete division of the cerebral hemispheres anteriorly, with fusion of the frontal lobes. The septum pellucidum is absent, and there is a dysgenic, hypoplastic corpus callosum. The single, fused frontal horn of the lateral ventricles is dilated, with the posterior atria measuring 12.5 mm.\n\nCortical sulcation is markedly delayed, showing a smooth cerebral surface abnormal for 22 weeks. Impression: Lobar holoprosencephaly with corpus callosum dysgenesis, ventriculomegaly, and severely delayed cortical sulcation."
