"diagnosis": "Cardiac MRI reveals severe, asymmetric septal hypertrophy of the left ventricle, with maximum wall thickness measuring 24 mm at the basal-to-mid anteroseptal segment. Left ventricular cavity size is small with hyperdynamic systolic function, resulting in an ejection fraction of 74%. Dynamic cine imaging demonstrates systolic anterior motion (SAM) of the mitral valve anterior leaflet, causing moderate mitral regurgitation.\n\nLate gadolinium enhancement (LGE) imaging demonstrates focal patchy enhancement at the right ventricular insertion points and within the hypertrophied septal segment. Impression: Classic findings of hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy (HOCM) with significant asymmetric septal hypertrophy, dynamic LVOT obstruction secondary to SAM, and associated myocardial fibrosis."
