"diagnosis": "The study demonstrates excessive trabeculation of the left ventricular apical and mid-lateral walls. In end-diastole, the ratio of non-compacted to compacted myocardium is calculated at 2.6, which meets criteria for non-compaction. Mild dilatation of the left ventricle is observed, with a mildly reduced ejection fraction of 47%.\n\nImpression: Left ventricular non-compaction (LVNC) cardiomyopathy with mild global systolic dysfunction. No evidence of myocardial infarction or gross fibrosis on late gadolinium enhancement."
