"diagnosis": "Three-dimensional magnetic resonance angiography (MRA) of the thoracic aorta demonstrates a focal narrowing of the descending thoracic aorta just distal to the origin of the left subclavian artery. Prominent intercostal and internal mammary collateral vessels are visualized bypassing the obstruction. Concentric hypertrophy of the left ventricle is present (mass index 112 g/m\u00b2) with an EF of 66%.\n\nImpression: Classic post-ductal coarctation of the aorta with extensive collateral circulation and secondary concentric left ventricular hypertrophy."
